    "result_text": "All tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`), including the new `coreReturnsFiscalYear` acceptance test. The full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI moved date-derived values to a fiscal-year basis (fiscal year starting 1 July, labelled by the calendar year it ends \u2014 the Australian convention matching the app's NSW/VIC/QLD domain, e.g. 1 Jul 2025\u201330 Jun 2026 is FY26).\n\n**New unit \u2014 `model/FiscalYear.java`** (single responsibility: fiscal-year math, reused everywhere):\n- `of(date)` \u2014 the ending calendar year of the fiscal year containing a date\n- `labelOf(date)` \u2014 formats `FY<YY>`\n- `elapsedBetween(from, to)` \u2014 whole fiscal years elapsed (July-1 boundaries crossed)\n\n**`model/Owner.java`**:\n- Added `getFiscalYear()` \u2192 `FY<YY>` from the business-day-adjusted registration date (null when no date), which MapStruct maps onto the DTO automatically.\n- Replaced `getTenureDays()` with `getTenureFiscalYears()`, and `getMembershipPoints()` now grants the long-tenure bonus for tenure of more than one fiscal year (was `> 365` days). Removed the now-unused `ChronoUnit` import.\n\n**`rest/validation/MembershipNumberGenerator.java`**: the `-M<YY>` year segment now derives from `FiscalYear.of(registrationDate)` instead of the raw registration year.\n\n**`resources/openapi.yml`**: added the read-only `fiscalYear` field to the owner schema so `OwnerDto` exposes it, and updated the `membershipNumber` / `membershipPoints` descriptions to reflect the fiscal-year basis. Kept `MembershipPoints` docs in sync.\n\nThe audit log confirmed the behaviour change end-to-end: a 2026-09-16 registration (after 1 July) now yields `membershipNumber=...-M27` and `fiscalYear=FY27`.\n\nOne judgment call worth flagging: the spec said tenure moves to \"elapsed fiscal years\" but didn't restate the bonus threshold, so I preserved the original \"more than one year\" intent as `> 1` elapsed fiscal year. Say the word if you'd prefer `>= 1` (any boundary crossed).",
